WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.562
Last, prove it works.

2
00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:05.823
Continuous monitoring is a
pipeline: emit, normalize,

3
00:00:05.823 --> 00:00:10.762
correlate, bind each record to
its control, report, and respond.

4
00:00:10.762 --> 00:00:13.187
The metrics are built
so they can't flatter.

5
00:00:13.187 --> 00:00:18.959
Detection coverage counts how many of
M-26-14's eleven baseline activities

6
00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:24.450
have an enabled, tested rule over a
fresh source, not how many rules exist.

7
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:30.288
Telemetry completeness treats a stale
required source as an AU-5 failure.

8
00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:36.388
KEV remediation counts closures within
the BOD 26-04 timeline, plus open items

9
00:00:36.388 --> 00:00:42.675
past it, because a share of the open queue
improves every time new findings arrive.

10
00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:47.337
And configuration reports passing,
failing and excepted settings separately.

11
00:00:47.337 --> 00:00:49.224
Read outside scores carefully.

12
00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:52.652
M-26-14 scores each system
at its lowest element,

13
00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:58.275
and a system can reach Advanced while
missing the six-month searchable floor.

14
00:00:58.275 --> 00:01:02.616
FedRAMP's 46 Key Security
Indicators bind cloud providers,

15
00:01:02.616 --> 00:01:07.488
not agencies; the agency reviews
each provider's quarterly report.

16
00:01:07.488 --> 00:01:09.846
A finding closes on re-test evidence,

17
00:01:09.846 --> 00:01:13.510
or the authorizing official
carries it with an end date.
